@startuml

title The step command

class "step command" as step_command <<message>> #E1F5FF {
    +step identifier : text
    +instance identifier : text
    +tenant : tenant id
    +payload : text
}

note top of step_command
Dispatches one step: the engine tells a handler what to do and which run it serves.
- step identifier: the step's stable identity, echoed by its completion.
- instance identifier: the run the step belongs to.
- tenant: the tenant the run acts for.
- payload: the work the operation performs, built from the
  run's request and the results so far.
end note

@enduml
